WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.482
Anthropic built a

00:00:01.293 --> 00:00:02.519
honeypot to catch

00:00:02.331 --> 00:00:03.663
rogue AI agents

00:00:04.182 --> 00:00:05.821
Researchers built Siren

00:00:05.939 --> 00:00:07.224
a honeypot test

00:00:07.048 --> 00:00:08.108
that puts agents

00:00:07.920 --> 00:00:09.665
in realistic simulations

00:00:09.665 --> 00:00:10.667
designed to tempt

00:00:10.479 --> 00:00:11.917
them into misbehaving

00:00:12.454 --> 00:00:13.550
How they respond

00:00:13.362 --> 00:00:14.847
helps researchers judge

00:00:14.659 --> 00:00:15.637
how likely new

00:00:15.449 --> 00:00:16.298
models are to

00:00:16.110 --> 00:00:16.840
go rogue in

00:00:16.652 --> 00:00:17.571
the real world

00:00:17.572 --> 00:00:18.739
and whether safety

00:00:18.551 --> 00:00:19.529
measures work

00:00:20.054 --> 00:00:21.292
The newest models

00:00:21.351 --> 00:00:23.013
Claude 5.5 and

00:00:22.825 --> 00:00:24.582
Claude Mythos 5.2

00:00:24.771 --> 00:00:25.478
fell for it

00:00:25.420 --> 00:00:27.129
only 0.6 to

00:00:26.941 --> 00:00:28.485
1.6 percent of the

00:00:28.297 --> 00:00:28.839
time

00:00:29.052 --> 00:00:29.995
while an earlier

00:00:29.806 --> 00:00:30.938
model went rogue

00:00:30.750 --> 00:00:32.671
25.8 percent of the

00:00:32.483 --> 00:00:33.108
time

00:00:33.630 --> 00:00:34.644
Full story on

00:00:34.455 --> 00:00:35.351
the dashboard
